     "part_tier": null,
     "problem_md": "A car of mass 800 kg is travelling in a straight line at a constant speed of 12 m/s. A constant resultant force then acts on the car causing the speed to increase.\n\nAfter 5.0 s, the speed of the car is 20 m/s.\n\nWhat is the size of the resultant force acting on the car?",
     "solution_md": "**Final answer:** **The correct answer is C**\n\n- Acceleration = change in velocity ÷ time\n\n$a = \\frac{v-u}{t} = \\frac{20-12}{5.0}$\n\n$= 1 . 6 \\text{m} / \\text{s}^{2}$\n\n- Force = mass × acceleration\n\n$F = m a = 800 \\times 1 . 6$\n\n$= 1280 \\text{N}$",
